# Presentation file placement

Keep UI next to the **only** page that renders it. When a second page under `src/presentation/pages/` imports the same module, it is **shared** and must live under `src/presentation/shared/` (components, hooks, or utils as appropriate).

## Check imports

For any module the diff adds, moves, or newly shares across pages:

```bash
rg -n "pages/<feature>/components/<Module>" src
```

Ignore the module file itself and colocated tests. Classify remaining importers:

| Who imports it | Where the file belongs |
| --- | --- |
| Only `src/presentation/pages/<feature>/` | Stay under that page folder |
| Two or more features under `pages/` (e.g. `report` and `report-form`) | `shared/components/`, `shared/hooks/`, or `shared/utils/` |
| App-wide chrome (header, footer, modal shell, pagination) | `shared/components/` |

## Reference examples

- **Shared:** `AddCollaboratorModal`, `AddOrganizationModal` — used from report form and profile associations; belong in `shared/components/`.
- **Page-local:** `DiscardChangesModal`, `EditContactModal`, `EditPaymentModal`, `CollaboratorFormModal` — only the report form; stay under `pages/report-form/components/`.

When a change renders an existing page-local module from a second page, **move** it to `shared/` in the same change. Do not leave it under the first page because it was written there first.

Tests stay colocated with the module. Page code may import `shared/` freely. Do not flag `shared/` importing a helper that only one feature owns unless this change is what made that helper shared.
